        <p>Births.</p>
        <p>O'BRlEN.—September 4, at Holly Bank, Great Sankey. the wife of Leonard Patrick O'Brien, of a son.</p>
        <p>Marriages. CLAY—BRODIE.--On the 31st August, at St. John's Presbyterian Church, by the Rev. Wm. Reid, Walter Adnah, son of George Clay, of War- rington, to Annie Thorburn, daughter of James Brodie, of Musselburgh. At home October 9th, Park Buildings. MACBETIC—BOYLE.—On Wednesday, the 2nd inst., at Our Lady's, Latchford, by the Rev. Father Tallon, Joseph Maxfield Macbeth, of Fair- field-road, Stockton Heath, to Elizabeth Mary (Lily) Boyle, only daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Alban Boyle, of Sycamore-terrace, Knutsford- road, Warrington.</p>
        <p>Deaths. TWISS.—On Tuesday, September Ist, 1914, at 18, Grove-street, Jane, the beloved wife of the late Mr. Edward Twiss, aged 75 years. Interment at Hill Cliffe, Saturday afternoon. WATBINS.—August 29th, at 80, Ellesmere-street, George Watkins, aged 48 years. MARSH.—August 28th, at 10, Wellington-street, Alice Marsh, aged 75 years. PRESTON.—August 29th, at 41, Cumberland-street, William Preston, aged 53 years.</p>
