      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-09-05_WidnesExaminer_art0223" n="art0223">
        <p>VOLKESTONE.—Foster's Castle Boarding Establishment and Temperance Hotel. Unique accommodation for visitors. Established 50 years. Junction Station. Personal attendance.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-09-05_WidnesExaminer_art0224" n="art0224">
        <head>Apartments, Furnished Houses, &amp;e.</head>
        <p>Apartments, Furnished Houses, &amp;e.</p>
        <p>APARTMENTS. —Centre Promenade; every attention; good cooking; terms moderate; highly recommended.—Stevens, 2, Mostyn Crescent, Llandudno.</p>
        <p>APARTMENTS, superior; cleanliness; good plain • cooking; adults only.—Mrs. Frost, 6, I Beckenham-road, Marine Park, New' Brighton.</p>
        <p>BISPIIAM, near Blackpool.—Public and Private Apartments; half minute sea and tram.—Misses Makin (from Bolton), 13, Hesketh- avenue.</p>
        <p>COI,WYN BAY.—Apartments, minute sea; open and bracing situation; splendid views; board if desired.—Mrs. Bedley-Vickers, Barcroft, Prince's Drive.</p>
        <p>COMFORTABLE Apartments for one or two gentlemen; front bed and sitting room; one minute from ear.-24, Padgate-lane, Warrington.</p>
        <p>DOUGLAS.— Apartments : Beds, 25.; full board, 255. week.—Mrs. Callin, 7, Laureston- terrace, Broadway, near shore.</p>
        <p>J' ARROGATE.—HiIIside Holiday Residences, pleasantly situated. central, near baths; from ss.—Apply Miss Fitton. JJARROGATE. Kingsley Hotel-Pension, Cold Bath-road. Central. Very moderate terms. Tel. 272.</p>
        <p>L ONDON VISITORS.—Bed and Breakfast, single up from 2s. 6d.; Double from 38. 6d.— Handel House, Handel-street, Russell-square. W.C.</p>
        <p>LLi!IN</p>
        <p>Rl-IYL.—Apartments, 8 doors from Prome- nade.—Mrs. Robinson, Ivy Dene, 16, River- street (late Birmingham).</p>
        <p>- - • CARBOROUGH.—Apartments, Mrs. Mier- -1.3 man, 7, Tollergate; 3 minutes from North and South Bays.</p>
        <p>SCARBOROUGH.—Apartments, Private and Public; 12, Royal Avenue, South Cliff; near Spa. Esplanade. Sea. Station, Gardens.</p>
        <p>SOUTHPORT. Comfortable Apartments, Public or Private; near town; all conveniences; piano.—Evans. 16. Tiensington-road.</p>
        <p>SOUTHPORT.—Apartments, near Promenade, Lord-street; bath, piano; moderate.—Mrs. and Miss Ibbotson, 53, West-street.</p>
        <p>SOUTIIPORT.—Mrs. Jackson, 36, Bold-street, 2 doors promenade; public and private apart- ments; board optional; moderate.</p>
        <p>SOUTllPORT.—Convalescents, elderly, holi- day, or permanent guests received; modern conveniences; terms moderate.—" Nurse," 8, Part- street.</p>
        <p>SOUTHPORT.—Mrs. Simpson, 9, Bank- square, Promenade (late Wesley-street). Apart- ments, with or without board; bath, piano, beds, and attendance, 2s. 6d. nightly.</p>
        <p>SOUTHPORT.—Mre. Rymer, 28, Princess- street. Public Apartments, near Band and both Stations. Good cooking; lofty rooms.</p>
