        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. The Sanitary Works Committee is pre- pared to receive TENDERS for the supply of 12,500 Second-hand BAGS, 38in. by 28in., to hold newts. each, and 1,000 Second-hand BAGS, 36in. by 24in., to hold lcwt. each. Samples may be seen and Tender Form obtained from the Manager, Longford Depot, Warrington. Tenders, in securely fastened envelopes, en- dorsed "Tender for Bags," and addressed "The Chairman, Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington, to be delivered not later than Monday, 14th September, 1914. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. RICHARD WILSON, Manager. Longford Depot, Warrington. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. ELECTRICITY DEPARTMENT. The Electricity and Tramways Committee of the County Borough of Warrington invite TENDERS for PAINTING and CLEANING at ' the ELECTRICITY WORKS, HOWLEY. Specification and form of tender can be obtained from the undersigned on payment of One Guinea, which will be returned on receipt of a bona-fide tender. Five shillings each will be charged for extra copies of specification. Tenders, addressed to the Chairman of the Electricity and Tramways Committee, Town Hall, Warrington, must be sealed with wax and endorsed "Tender for Painting and Cleaning," and delivered not later than 12 o'clock noon on Tuesday, September 15th, 1914. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. F. V. L. MATHIAS, Borough Electrical &amp; Tramways Engineer. Howley, Warrington.</p>
