        <p>HE RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL OF T RUNCORN. PRIVATE STREET WORKS—WALTON INFERIOR. The Rural District Council of Runcorn invite TENDERS for the Making with Tarred Macadam of certain Streets and Passages in the parish of Walton Inferior within their district. Plans, specifications and quantities may be seen on application to Mr. Robert Garnett, Bold. street Chambers, Warrington, the Council's Sur- veyor, on or after the 7th day of September, 1914, and copies of quantities and forms of tender may be obtained from him on deposit of 10s. 6d., which will be returned on receipt of a bona-fide tender. Sealed tenders, endorsed "Tender for Private Street Works, Walton Inferior," to be delivered at my office not later than Monday, the 28th day of September. 1914. The Council do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender. By order, GEO. F. ASHTON, Clerk to the Council. 71, High-street, Runcorn, 4th September. 1914.</p>
