        <p>WARRINGTON UNION. TENDERS. PERSONS WILLING to contract for the supply of any of the undermentioned articles, to be delivered free of expense at the Workhouse, Warrington, or Cottage Homes, Padgate, at such times and in such quantities as the Guardians or their officers may require, are requested to send in Tenders to me on or before 10 a.m. on Wednesday, the 9th September, 1914, and the same will be considered by the Guard- ians at a meeting to be held on the same date. Tenders are required : From Ist October, 1914, to 30th September, 1915 —Sweeping chimneys. From let October, 1914, to 31st March, 1915 : Coal and Slack Fish and Ice Clogs Groceries &amp; Necessaries Crockeryware Butchers' Meat Boots, Shoes and Flour and Oatmeal Slippers Drapery Coffins Wines, Spirits, Beer Brooms and Brushes and Stout Leather &amp; Shoemakers' Drugs Necessaries Dressings Tailors' Goods Soda Water Butter, Bacon, Cheese, Paints, &amp;c. Lard, Margarine, &amp;c. Ironmongery Mackintosh Sheeting Thirds Tobacco and Snuff Electrical Goods Separate tenders must be sent for the Work- house and Cottage Homes, and samples of the articles required can be seen at either Institu- tions between the hours of 10 to 12 noon and 2 to 4 p.m. The fuel to be supplied must be according to the specification as set out on the tender form, and quotations must be made for delivery either to the siding adjoining the Workhouse, or by cart, and by cart to the Cottage Homes. Forms of tender, and instructions to persons tendering (which must be strictly complied with), may be obtained from the undersigned. All accounts will be paid monthly. The Guardians do not necessarily bind them- selves to accept the lowest or any tender. By order, ARTHUR BOTTOMLEY. Clerk to the Guardians. Bewsey Chambers, August 26th, 1914.</p>
