        <p>BOWLING. WARRINGTON WORKS' AMATEUR ASSOCIATION. \ - Annual Handicap. DRAW FOR THE FIRST HOIND. To be played this afternoon. As the handi- cap will be completed this day all winners are requested not to leave the green. • 2.0. W. Birchall, C (5) v. A. Gleave, Ws (Sc'.). E. Povei, By (5) v. W. Blackledge, P &amp; K (3). R. Deakin, G (5) v. H. Atherton, LW (3). W. Morgan, C &amp; J (4) V. W. Pointer, By (6)- W. Ashbrooke, CL (5) v. F. Burgess, WT (6). A. Holloway, LW (7) v. J. Miller, C (6). R. Allen, By (4) v. F. Howard, N (6). A. Davies, P &amp; K (6) v. J. Shaw, Ws (7). 2.25. J. Smith, WB (7) v. J. Simeock, C &amp; J (5). C. Jordan, CL (3) v. R. Barnett, P &amp; K (5). T. Clare, By (2) v. H. Hughes, 0 (7). T. Garnett, CL (5) v. S. Millett, WR (7). J. Pemberton, P &amp; K (4) 1. G. Cook, WR (7). H. Fogg, LW (5) v. J. Kieran, AA (5). W:.Thomason, MU (2) v. H. Green, FL (5). J. Cundall, PP (6) v. A. Houghton, CL (5). 2.50. J. Craddock, CL (7) v. J. I'ollard, PP (6). J. Spencer, P &amp; K (4) v. J. Litherland, WB (5). C. Tranter, MH (5) v. W. Holland, C &amp; J (6). T. Horrabin, L &amp; N.-W. (3) v. E. Coyne, PK (3) A. Warburton, Wx (1) V. E. Mannion, By (7). H. France, R. (4) V. W. Hitchmough, PP (5). E. Barnes, By (6) V. H. Broadhurst, C (2). F. Brandwood, P &amp; K (7) v. P. Wright, C (3). 3.15. H. Higliam, P &amp; K (1) v. E. Lunt, N (6). G. Leigh, Ws (5) v. T. Jackson, sen. Ws (5). J. Bibby, CL (4) v. G: Harrop, By (5). S. Garnett, By (6) v. R. Eyes, FM (5). , E. Rowlands, Wx (7) v. J. Barnard, N (6). J. Gibson, PP (4) v. J. Hankinson, CA (5). , H. Rushworth, P&amp; K (1) v. C. Perry, WR (4). E. Rowlands, CA (2) v. J. George, PP (6). TRAVELLERS v. LIBERAL CLUB. Pleasant Function at Bewsey-street • - Green. The Warrington and Widnes Commercial Travellers were entertained by the Liberal Club bowlers on Saturday, when a pleasant friendly match resulted in a 48-point victory for the home team. At the conclusion of the play the party ad- journed for tea, which was admirably served in the club by Mrs. Clay. • Councillor J. Wilkinson warmly welcomed the visitors, whom, he said, should arrange an an- nual fixture, and Mr. W. P. Ashton, who replied, said they hoped to make a better show next time. The afternoon's proceedings were ably ar- ranged by Mr. W. H. Owen, secretary for the Travellers, ,and Mr. George Marshall, of the Liberal Club., to whom thanks are due, and also to Mrs. Clay for her admirable catering. The scores were (Liberal Club names first) Councillor J. Wilkinson and T. Chriehley, 15; A. J. Allan and W. Walker, 2. P. Walker and J. Pollard. 8; F. Plumpton and - Devenal, 15. Jos. Wilkinson and Wm. Daintith, 15; H. Gorst and G. Box, 5. E. A. Sanders and T. Drew, 15; W. H. Owen and H. Mercer, 4. • J. Parsons and J. Pollitt. 12; S. Payne and T. Richardson, 15. P. Green and W. Farrington. 15; J. T. Smith and G. Eastwood, 3. J. George and J. Smith, 15; W. P. Ashton and C. Leigh, 7. M. Tobin and J. Feeney, 14; J. Poaser and E. Walker, H. T. O'Brien and Wm. Hayes, 15; G. Bowman and W. G. Hayes. 11. E. Lunf and J. Broadhurst, jun., 15; T. Man- ner ing and A. Greenhalgh, 10. 0. Vernon and G. Marshall, 11; G. Pendlebury and T. Pemberton, jun., 15. Total-Liberal Club, 150; Travellers, 102. Liberal Club won by 48 points. _ _ .</p>
